# .docpairs — the doc-implication map.
#
# Each line pairs a code surface with the document that describes it. The map
# is DATA for the judgment gate: when a pull request changes a path that
# literally starts with the prefix on the left, the document on the right is
# IMPLICATED — the judge receives its full content alongside the diff and
# rules on whether the change falsifies it. A falsified, un-updated implicated
# document is a bounce.
#
# Matching is literal string-prefix (the 2026-07-03 markup ruling amending
# ADR-0002): no glob semantics, nothing matches that the map did not name. An
# exact file path is its own prefix. The judge refuses a prefix carrying a
# glob metacharacter, loudly.
#
# Nothing mechanical counts touches against this file (ADR-0002: doc pairing
# binds through the judge). Keep pairs few and obviously true.
#
# Format: one pairing per line, "<path-prefix> -> <doc path>"; "#" comments.

pkg/httpapi/    -> docs/api.md
Taskfile.yml    -> docs/operations.md
config/         -> docs/operations.md
delight.yaml    -> docs/operations.md
